encode: reject video frames that do not match the encoder (CVE-2026-125204, -125212, -125218, -125235, -125260)

avcodec_send_frame() accepted a video frame of any size or pixel format, and
several video encoders then read past the frame. The check rejects a frame whose
size or format differs from the encoder's unless the encoder declares
AV_CODEC_CAP_PARAM_CHANGE. Only video encoders reach it, and this build has none
(its encoders are audio only), so it changes nothing here; it is carried so the
five CVEs it fixes are closed by source, not by argument.

Backport of FFmpeg master 254cebc4e8e1358ffcf7ba6fc13bcc4a98db80de (2026-10-20), 9b99973b2bbecee0b7e1e57035b95498b42f54a6 (PR 25682, merged 2026-11-05), not in n9.0.2.
Ported by hand: n9.0.2 has neither commit; the patch adds the check of the first
with the != comparison of the second, which is what master has.

diff --git a/libavcodec/encode.c b/libavcodec/encode.c
--- a/libavcodec/encode.c
+++ b/libavcodec/encode.c
@@ -517,6 +517,15 @@ static int encode_send_frame_internal(AVCodecContext *avctx, const AVFrame *src)
                 }
             }
         }
+    } else if (!(avctx->codec->capabilities & AV_CODEC_CAP_PARAM_CHANGE)) {
+        const AVPixFmtDescriptor *desc = av_pix_fmt_desc_get(src->format);
+
+        if (!(desc && desc->flags & AV_PIX_FMT_FLAG_HWACCEL) &&
+            (src->format != avctx->pix_fmt ||
+             src->width != avctx->width || src->height != avctx->height)) {
+            av_log(avctx, AV_LOG_ERROR, "Frame size or pixel format does not match the encoder\n");
+            return AVERROR(EINVAL);
+        }
     }
 
     ret = av_frame_ref(dst, src);
